---
import PlaygroundShell from '../../components/PlaygroundShell.astro';
---
<PlaygroundShell title="Which guard stops the overload?" hint="The gateway receives 300 queries: 240 from real apps and 60 abusive ones. The services can do a fixed amount of work. Switch the protections on and off and see which ones are needed.">
  <ol class="how">
    <li>The default has <b>batching on</b> and a <b>depth limit of 5</b>: the 30 queries that are 6 levels deep are rejected, but the 30 <b>wide</b> queries (4 levels with 10 items per list, 11,110 objects each) still run, and the services reach <b>158 %</b> of their capacity, so only <b>63 %</b> of the answers are served.</li>
    <li>Set <b>cost limit to 500</b>: both kinds of abusive query are rejected for their estimated cost, the real apps use <b>24 %</b> of capacity and all 240 are answered. A depth limit alone cannot see width.</li>
    <li>With the <b>cost limit</b> still 500 (depth limit 5), turn <b>batching off</b>: no abuse, but each query makes up to 111 calls (N+1) and the load is <b>195 %</b>. Persisted queries only also stops the abuse, but blocks the 15 ad hoc queries of real apps.</li>
  </ol>
  <div class="pg gqb" data-gqb>
    <div class="pg-row">
      <label>Fetch entities <select class="pg-in" data-batch><option value="1" selected>in batches (one call per level)</option><option value="0">one call per parent (N+1)</option></select></label>
      <label>Depth limit <select class="pg-in" data-depth><option value="0">none</option><option value="5" selected>5</option><option value="3">3</option></select></label>
      <label>Cost limit <select class="pg-in" data-cost><option value="0" selected>none</option><option value="500">500 objects</option></select></label>
      <label>Persisted queries only <select class="pg-in" data-pers><option value="0" selected>no</option><option value="1">yes</option></select></label>
    </div>
    <div class="pg-grid">
      <div class="pg-box" data-b1><h3>Service load</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-o1></span><span class="pg-note" data-n1></span></div>
      <div class="pg-box" data-b2><h3>Real queries answered</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-o2></span><span class="pg-note" data-n2></span></div>
      <div class="pg-box" data-b3><h3>Rejected at the gate</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-o3></span><span class="pg-note" data-n3></span></div>
    </div>
    <p class="pg-out" data-verdict aria-live="polite"></p>
    <p class="pg-note">Model: 300 queries. 180 &quot;feed&quot; queries (depth 4, cost 310, stored), 45 &quot;profile&quot; queries (depth 2, cost 110, stored), 15 ad hoc feed queries that are not stored, 30 wide abusive queries (depth 4, cost 11,110) and 30 deep abusive ones (depth 6, cost 1,111,110). Work is 20 units for each service call plus 1 unit for each object, and the services can do 250,000 units. If the load is above capacity, every executed query is served with the same share of them failing. A depth limit rejects a query deeper than the limit, and a cost limit rejects a query above it.</p>
  </div>
</PlaygroundShell>
<script>
  import { query, fmt } from '../../playground';
  document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-gqb]').forEach((root) => {
    const q = query(root);
    const num = (s: string) => Number(q<HTMLSelectElement>(s).value);
    const CAP = 250000; const OVER = 20; const LEGIT = 240;
    // n: how many of the 300 queries; reg: stored; calls without and with batching
    const KINDS = [
      { n: 180, legit: true, reg: true, depth: 4, cost: 310, objs: 210, naive: 111, bat: 3 },
      { n: 45, legit: true, reg: true, depth: 2, cost: 110, objs: 110, naive: 11, bat: 2 },
      { n: 15, legit: true, reg: false, depth: 4, cost: 310, objs: 210, naive: 111, bat: 3 },
      { n: 30, legit: false, reg: false, depth: 4, cost: 11110, objs: 11110, naive: 1111, bat: 4 },
      { n: 30, legit: false, reg: false, depth: 6, cost: 1111110, objs: 1111110, naive: 111111, bat: 6 },
    ];
    const TOTAL = KINDS.reduce((a, k) => a + k.n, 0); // 300 queries
    const LEGIT_MAX_CALLS = Math.max(...KINDS.filter((k) => k.legit).map((k) => k.naive));
    function draw() {
      const batch = num('[data-batch]') === 1; const depth = num('[data-depth]'); const cost = num('[data-cost]'); const pers = num('[data-pers]') === 1;
      let ranLegit = 0; let ranAbuse = 0; let units = 0; let blockedLegit = 0; let rejected = 0; let rPers = 0; let rDepth = 0; let rCost = 0;
      for (const k of KINDS) {
        const why = pers && !k.reg ? 'p' : depth && k.depth > depth ? 'd' : cost && k.cost > cost ? 'c' : '';
        if (why) { rejected += k.n; if (k.legit) blockedLegit += k.n; if (why === 'p') rPers += k.n; else if (why === 'd') rDepth += k.n; else rCost += k.n; continue; }
        if (k.legit) ranLegit += k.n; else ranAbuse += k.n;
        units += k.n * ((batch ? k.bat : k.naive) * OVER + k.objs);
      }
      const load = Math.round((units * 100) / CAP); const served = units <= CAP ? 1 : CAP / units; const answered = Math.floor(ranLegit * served);
      q('[data-o1]').textContent = `${fmt(load)} % of capacity`; q('[data-n1]').textContent = `${fmt(units)} units of work, ${ranAbuse} abusive queries ran`;
      q('[data-o2]').textContent = `${answered} of ${LEGIT}`; q('[data-n2]').textContent = blockedLegit ? `${blockedLegit} real queries were rejected by a guard` : 'no real query was rejected by a guard';
      q('[data-o3]').textContent = `${rejected} of ${TOTAL}`; q('[data-n3]').textContent = `persisted ${rPers}, depth ${rDepth}, cost ${rCost}`;
      q<HTMLElement>('[data-b1]').style.setProperty('--c', load <= 100 ? 'var(--good)' : 'var(--bad)');
      q<HTMLElement>('[data-b2]').style.setProperty('--c', answered === LEGIT ? 'var(--good)' : 'var(--bad)');
      q<HTMLElement>('[data-b3]').style.setProperty('--c', 'var(--accent)');
      const out = q('[data-verdict]'); const bad = load > 100 || blockedLegit > 0; out.classList.toggle('bad', bad);
      out.textContent = load > 100
        ? (ranAbuse > 0 ? `Overloaded: ${ranAbuse} abusive queries got through and the services are at ${load} %, so only ${Math.round(served * 100)} % of answers are served. Look for the guard that sees what the abuse looks like.` : `Overloaded by the real queries alone: with one call per parent they make up to ${LEGIT_MAX_CALLS} calls each and the services are at ${load} %. Batching fixes this.`)
        : blockedLegit > 0 ? `The services are fine at ${load} %, but ${blockedLegit} real queries are rejected. This guard is too strict for the apps.` : `Healthy: ${load} % of capacity, no abusive query ran and all ${LEGIT} real queries were answered.`;
    }
    root.addEventListener('input', draw); root.addEventListener('change', draw);
    draw();
  });
</script>
